---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — HubHum"
  description="Privacy-by-design disclosure for HubHum and the HubHum Chrome Extension (Manifest V3), including optional IP-anonymized GA4 analytics and 1-click browser opt-out."
>
  <div class="container detail-wrap">
    <a href={withBase('/')} class="breadcrumb">← Back to HubHum Catalog</a>

    <section class="article-card" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="hero-badge" style="margin-bottom:0.85rem;">
        <span>Chrome Web Store Compliant • Single Purpose &amp; Limited Use</span>
      </div>
      <h1 style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.1rem);">
        Privacy Policy — HubHum &amp; Chrome Extension
      </h1>
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.4rem;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.92rem;">
        Last updated: <strong>{lastUpdated}</strong> • Bilingual Official Notice (EN / IT)
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.4rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        1. English — Privacy &amp; Data Usage Disclosure
      </h2>
      <p>
        HubHum (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;HubHum – A Git Hub for Humans&rdquo;) respects your privacy and follows strict{' '}
        <strong>privacy-by-design</strong> and <strong>zero-leak</strong> principles across both our static web catalog
        and the official Chrome Extension (Manifest V3).
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Active Public URL Only:</strong> The extension only reads the active browser tab URL when you visit a
          public GitHub repository page (<code>https://github.com/:owner/:repo</code>) or click the{' '}
          <em>&ldquo;Humanize with HubHum&rdquo;</em> action button or extension popup. We never read page form inputs,
          private repositories, browsing history outside GitHub repository URLs, or personal account tokens.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Profiling, Zero Sale, Zero PII:</strong> We do not collect, store, sell, transfer, or monetize any
          Personally Identifiable Information (PII), IP logs, health/financial data, or authentication credentials.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Web Traffic Analytics (Google Tag Manager &amp; GA4):</strong> HubHum loads container{' '}
          <code>GTM-NNT4QBLT</code> (<code>googletagmanager.com/gtm.js</code>) asynchronously via Google Tag Manager{' '}
          and supports Google Analytics 4 (<code>gtag.js</code> when <code>PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID</code> is set) and
          Cloudflare Web Analytics solely to measure aggregated page views, referral sources, and popular software
          guides. IP anonymization is enabled (<code>anonymize_ip: true</code>), Google Signals and ad personalization
          remain disabled, and local extension/favorite preferences (<code>localStorage</code> /{' '}
          <code>chrome.storage.local</code>) never leave your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How to Disable / Opt Out:</strong> You can disable both GTM (<code>GTM-NNT4QBLT</code>) and GA4 at
          any time using your browser&apos;s tracking protection, the{' '}
          <a
            href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            style="color:var(--accent-fg-text);text-decoration:underline;"
          >
            Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on
          </a>, or our instant browser opt-out toggle below (stored locally as <code>hubhum_ga_optout</code>), which
          blocks loading of the tag container cleanly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Single Purpose &amp; Limited Use Compliance:</strong> All requested permissions (<code>activeTab</code>,{' '}
          <code>storage</code>, and <code>notifications</code>) are used exclusively to detect a public GitHub project,
          convert its documentation via our serverless bridge (
          <code>https://hubhum-api-bridge.keomadavanzo.workers.dev/api/convert</code>), and notify you when the guide
          is live. Data handling strictly complies with the Chrome Web Store Developer Program Policy, including Limited
          Use requirements.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Affiliate Transparency (#ad):</strong> Some recommended tool links inside software guides include an
          anonymous partner referral tag (SubID) so HubHum can remain free. No personal user data is transmitted via
          these links.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.8rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        2. Italiano — Informativa Privacy &amp; Trattamento Dati
      </h2>
      <p>
        HubHum (&ldquo;HubHum – A Git Hub for Humans&rdquo;) adotta principi rigorosi di <strong>privacy-by-design</strong>{' '}
        e <strong>zero-tracking</strong> sia sul catalogo web statico sia sull&apos;estensione ufficiale Google Chrome
        (Manifest V3).
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Lettura del solo URL pubblico su azione utente:</strong> L&apos;estensione legge esclusivamente l&apos;URL
          pubblico della scheda attiva su <code>https://github.com/:owner/:repo</code> per verificare se il software è già
          presente su HubHum o avviare la conversione in guida semplice su tua esplicita richiesta. Non accede mai a
          repository privati, credenziali, email o cronologia di navigazione personale.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Statistiche di traffico (Google Tag Manager &amp; GA4):</strong> Il sito HubHum utilizza in modo
          asincrono il contenitore Google Tag Manager <code>GTM-NNT4QBLT</code> (<code>googletagmanager.com/gtm.js</code>)
          insieme a Google Analytics 4 (<code>gtag.js</code>) e Cloudflare Web Analytics esclusivamente per rilevare visite
          aggregate, provenienza del traffico e guide più consultate, con anonimizzazione IP e personalizzazione annunci
          disattivate. Nessuna profilazione PII, nessun remarketing e nessun accesso ai preferiti locali (
          <code>localStorage</code> / <code>chrome.storage.local</code>). Il controllo opt-out qui sotto (
          <code>hubhum_ga_optout=1</code>) impedisce il caricamento sia di GTM sia di GA4.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conformità Chrome Web Store (Single Purpose &amp; Limited Use):</strong> I permessi{' '}
          <code>activeTab</code>, <code>storage</code> e <code>notifications</code> servono unicamente allo scopo
          dichiarato dell&apos;estensione: tradurre schede software open-source in guide chiare e avvisarti con una
          notifica desktop al completamento.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div
        style="margin-top:1.5rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--surface-muted);"
      >
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.4rem;font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--text);">
          Analytics Opt-Out Preference (This Browser)
        </h2>
        <p id="ga-optout-status" style="margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);">
          Loading analytics preference...
        </p>
        <button type="button" id="ga-optout-btn" class="btn btn-outline">
          Disable Analytics (GTM &amp; GA4) in This Browser
        </button>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.8rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        3. Contact &amp; Takedown Requests
      </h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or open-source project takedown requests, contact the maintainer via{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/DavanzoKeoma/HubHum"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          style="color:var(--accent-fg-text);text-decoration:underline;"
        >
          DavanzoKeoma/HubHum on GitHub
        </a>{' '}
        or email <code>keomadavanzo@gmail.com</code>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const optOutBtn = document.getElementById('ga-optout-btn') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
    const optOutStatus = document.getElementById('ga-optout-status');

    function isOptedOut(): boolean {
      try {
        return localStorage.getItem('hubhum_ga_optout') === '1';
      } catch {
        return false;
      }
    }

    function syncOptOutUi() {
      const disabled = isOptedOut();
      if (optOutStatus) {
        optOutStatus.textContent = disabled
          ? 'Current status: Google Tag Manager (GTM-NNT4QBLT) and GA4 are DISABLED in this browser (hubhum_ga_optout=1).'
          : 'Current status: IP-anonymized analytics (GTM-NNT4QBLT / GA4) are allowed on this site (hubhum_ga_optout=0).';
      }
      if (optOutBtn) {
        optOutBtn.textContent = disabled
          ? 'Re-enable Analytics in This Browser'
          : 'Disable Analytics (GTM & GA4) in This Browser';
      }
    }

    syncOptOutUi();
    optOutBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      try {
        localStorage.setItem('hubhum_ga_optout', isOptedOut() ? '0' : '1');
      } catch {}
      syncOptOutUi();
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
